{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2672 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d93a9dd560c324d878e9799f8df79fd16efc770896518292cb13c777cfbb8f96" :edb/db-before-t 2671 :edb/db-after-t 2672 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535984 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:15:56.308Z" 13194139535984 true] [17592186133797 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378209 13194139535984 true] [17592186133798 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378216 13194139535984 true] [17592186133798 1020 #edb/ref 17592186378223 13194139535984 true] [17592186134482 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535984 true] [17592186134482 1100 "Let $V = R_{2}[t]$, the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n$⟨p(t), q(t)⟩ = p(-1)q(-1) + p(0)q(0) + p(1)q(1)$.\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V$:\n\n$p_{1}(t) = t^{2} - t, p_{2}(t) = t^{2} + t, q(t) = 4t^{2} - t - 1$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S = Span{p_{1}(t), p_{2}(t)}$ given that $p_{1}(t)⊥p_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $Span{p_{1}(t)}$ equals $2t^{2} - 2t$." 13194139535984 false] [17592186134482 1100 "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $2,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}-t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,q(t)=4{t}^{2}-t-1\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t)}$ equals $2{t}^{2}-2t.$" 13194139535984 true] [17592186134482 1145 "Since the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)=2{t}^{2}-2t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{p}_{2}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t)=\\frac{⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{p}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =q(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+q(0){p}_{2}(0)+q(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{-1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{-1}+(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{0}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{0}+(4{t}^{2}\\,-\\,t\\,-\\,1){|}_{1}\\,\\,\\cdot \\,({t}^{2}\\,+\\,t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={p}_{2}(-1){p}_{2}(-1)+{p}_{2}(0){p}_{2}(0)+{p}_{2}(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{-1}+({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{0}+({t}^{2}+t)^{2}{|}_{1} \\\\  & ={0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) & =\\frac{4}{4}\\cdot ({t}^{2}+t)={t}^{2}+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-2t+({t}^{2}+t) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378209 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378210 13194139535984 true] [17592186378209 1089 "q-105219" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378209 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535984 true] [17592186378209 1100 "Let $V=C[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the vector space of continuous functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$, and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(t)=1,\\,{f}_{2}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,g(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ given that ${f}_{1}(t)⊥{f}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{2}(t)}$ equals $-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378209 1113 #uuid "d54a1f9d-2365-54c2-8a4e-cb77c343af4b" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378209 1145 "Since the set ${{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{2}(t)}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $g(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}{{f}_{1}(t)}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)=\\frac{⟨g(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩}{⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩}\\,{f}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨g(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }g(t){f}_{1}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+3t]_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(2-0+3\\pi )-(2-0-3\\pi ) \\\\  & =6\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{f}_{1}(t),{f}_{1}(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }1\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t) & =\\frac{6\\pi }{2\\pi }\\cdot 1=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,g(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{1}(t)}\\,g(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{f}_{2}(t)}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378211 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378212 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378213 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378214 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378215 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1041 "selection" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378211 13194139535984 true] [17592186378210 1110 #uuid "b1286aba-efef-5fe2-97da-4e03cd0da572" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378211 1034 "3-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378211 1111 #uuid "41ff7c3b-ff01-569e-bc92-5e757efff761" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378212 1034 "6+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378212 1111 #uuid "ae899bdb-3836-5da7-856c-855a176f5abf" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378213 1034 "3-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378213 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378213 1111 #uuid "6b190447-c8cc-53ba-a39e-869dd35a2752" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378214 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378214 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378214 1111 #uuid "0cce0153-36f5-560a-90f5-1f3f35269b1e" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378215 1034 "3+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378215 1111 #uuid "147561c7-14e4-508e-a5dd-cbee2d129aed" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378216 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378217 13194139535984 true] [17592186378216 1089 "q-105496" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378216 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535984 true] [17592186378216 1100 "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=3t+2$ with respect to the inner product." 13194139535984 true] [17592186378216 1113 #uuid "49ea9adf-d0b5-5c27-8ee7-8550fea7b78d" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378216 1145 "The distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=3t+2$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-g(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-3-(3t+2)‖ \\\\  & =‖5t-5‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨5t-5,5t-5⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨5t-5,5t-5⟩ & =(5t-5){|}_{0}\\cdot (5t-5){|}_{0}+(5t-5){|}_{1}\\cdot (5t-5){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{25}=5.$" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378218 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378219 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378220 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378221 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378222 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1041 "selection" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378222 13194139535984 true] [17592186378217 1110 #uuid "a39d2211-f1c8-5cd4-88a1-1a597eefbe6b" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378218 1034 "11" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378218 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378218 1111 #uuid "3c03425b-e8c6-5e76-b608-573ae3e46d22" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378219 1034 "3" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378219 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378219 1111 #uuid "8c3accac-fdf3-5750-b0b8-a663f8235898" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378220 1034 "2" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378220 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378220 1111 #uuid "667a123d-774c-54e8-b69f-4fde26874f4e" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378221 1034 "1" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378221 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378221 1111 #uuid "f84b4bb4-3104-5dfc-b7a5-1c6691c1287c" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378222 1034 "5" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378222 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535984 true] [17592186378222 1111 #uuid "f901e143-9b26-575a-9f23-13f61cad5cd4" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378223 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378224 13194139535984 true] [17592186378223 1089 "q-105498" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378223 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535984 true] [17592186378223 1100 "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=2t-1$ with respect to the inner product." 13194139535984 true] [17592186378223 1113 #uuid "f12a29fb-7c8e-5ef7-b086-14df38ba86c6" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378223 1145 "The distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=2t-1$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-g(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-3-(2t-1)‖ \\\\  & =‖6t-2‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨6t-2,6t-2⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨6t-2,6t-2⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6t-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{t}^{2}-24t+4)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[12{t}^{3}-12{t}^{2}+4t]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(12-12+4)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{4}=2.$" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378225 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378226 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378227 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378228 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378229 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1041 "selection" 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378226 13194139535984 true] [17592186378224 1110 #uuid